      <node concept="Xl_RD" id="5NJc6w6F60G" role="33vP2m">
        <property role="Xl_RC" value="Alters MPS language structure: create concepts/enums, manage and rename properties/children/references. Returns a JSON object with 'ok':true and 'data':{...} on success, or 'ok':false and 'error':\&quot;...\&quot; on failure. Parameters are passed as a JSON object string. For CREATE_CONCEPTS with make:true the response includes makeStatus (\&quot;success\&quot;, \&quot;runtime_stale\&quot;, \&quot;failed\&quot; or \&quot;skipped\&quot;), verified against the live runtime: \&quot;success\&quot; means the build succeeded AND every created concept's runtime descriptor read back non-hollow, so dependent tools can be trusted immediately. \&quot;runtime_stale\&quot; lists the still-hollow concept names in hollowConcepts together with a descriptorRecoveryAction." />
      </node>
      <node concept="3Tm6S6" id="5NJc6w6F60H" role="1B3o_S" />
    </node>
