    <node concept="Wx3nA" id="5NJc6w6GrTv" role="jymVt">
      <property role="TrG5h" value="PARSE_JAVA_AND_INSERT_TOOL_SPEC_DESCR" />
      <property role="3TUv4t" value="true" />
      <node concept="3uibUv" id="5NJc6w6GrTw" role="1tU5fm">
        <ref role="3uigEE" to="wyt6:~String" resolve="String" />
      </node>
      <node concept="Xl_RD" id="5NJc6w6GrTx" role="33vP2m">
        <property role="Xl_RC" value="[generic] parses Java code with the MPS JavaParser and inserts the result as MPS nodes - as project model root(s), as a child in a given role, or as a replacement of an existing node. parameters is a JSON object: code (max 50000 chars), featureKind (CLASS, CLASS_CONTENT, FIELD, METHOD, NESTED_CLASS, STATEMENTS or EXPRESSION; CLASS_STUB is rejected), optional recovery (default true), optional contextNodeRef (required for FIELD/METHOD/NESTED_CLASS/CLASS_CONTENT to supply the target Classifier), insert (mode 'root' with modelRef, 'child' with parentRef and role and optional position, or 'replace' with targetRef; optional virtualPackage for root), and optional postProcess (importUsedLanguages, resolveReferences; both default true). Root insertion always appends and rejects a position other than -1 or absent; replace requires exactly one top-level parsed node; child insertion into a single-cardinality role overwrites the existing occupant, and into a multi-cardinality role a position past the child count is clamped to an append, with each inserted node reporting its actual index. Unrecognized keys, including dryRun, are rejected. Java 8+ constructs the MPS parser recognizes are mapped to the matching BaseLanguage extension - notably lambdas, which become closures. Every success envelope carries a problems array listing the type-system errors and warnings found within the inserted nodes, empty when the insert type-checks. port note: insert.mode 'console' is not supported, because the MPS Console integration was dropped from this port; the insert runs in a write action rather than an undoable command." />
      </node>
      <node concept="3Tm6S6" id="5NJc6w6GrTy" role="1B3o_S" />
    </node>
